---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **작품 수와 읽힘, 그리고 그 사다리가 한 사람에 대해 말하는 것.**
 * (`/works-and-readers`)
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **사다리만 내지 않는다.** 가운데값 일곱 배 옆에 반드시 「한 사람 확률 81.8%」를 둔다.
 *    사다리는 무리의 성질이고, 손님이 알고 싶은 것은 대개 한 사람이다.
 * ⛔ **방향을 말하지 않는다.** 작품이 읽힘을 부른 것인지 그 반대인지 못 가른다.
 * ⛔ **겹침을 감추지 않는다.** 1편인 배우 열에 하나가 5편이상의 가운데를 넘는다.
 * ⛔ **날것의 사다리를 그대로 안 쓴다.** 합계는 문서가 있는 판만 더한 수라
 *    「많이 읽힌다」와 「판이 더 많다」가 섞여 있다. 한 판만 본 수를 나란히 싣는다.
 * ⛔ **「네 판 다 있는 사람끼리」로 맞추지 않는다.** 그것은 읽힘의 뒤에 오는 것이라
 *    그것으로 나누면 무리가 바뀐다(collider). 그 수는 보이되 가운데값을 안 뽑는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwCardnews from '../../components/KcwCardnews.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-works-and-readers.json';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';

const 아래 = d.bands[0];
const 위 = d.bands[d.bands.length - 1];
const 한판확률 = Math.round(1000 * d.personLevel.oneEdition) / 10;
const 합확률 = Math.round(1000 * d.personLevel.summed) / 10;
const 겹 = d.overlap.oneEdition;

const TITLE = 'Actors with five charting titles are read seven times as often, '
  + 'and that still tells you little about any one of them';
const DESC =
  `Across ${d.actorsMeasured} Korean actors on four Southeast Asian Wikipedias, the median `
  + `reader count rises at every step from one charting title to five or more. Pick one actor `
  + `from each end and the busier one is read more ${한판확률}% of the time.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org/', 'https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/works-and-readers">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Of {d.actorsMeasured} Korean actors we can measure, those with one charting title are read
    {' '}<b>{아래.oneEdition.median}</b> times per million reads of the Indonesian Wikipedia. Those
    with five or more are read <b>{위.oneEdition.median}</b>. The median rises at every step in
    between. Now pick one actor from each of those two groups at random: the busier one is the
    more-read one <b>{한판확률}%</b> of the time.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The ladder</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Two columns, because one of them is misleading on its own. The <em>summed</em> column adds an
      actor's reads across the editions that have an article about them — and actors with more
      titles have articles in more editions, so that column is partly counting coverage. The
      {' '}<em>one edition</em> column holds coverage constant by looking only at the
      {' '}{d.editionNames ? d.editionNames[d.controlEdition] : d.controlEdition} Wikipedia.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Charting titles</th><th>Actors</th><th>Summed across editions</th>
            <th>One edition only</th><th>Has all four articles</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.bands.map((b) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{b.label}</td>
              <td class="fine">{b.actors}</td>
              <td>{b.summed.median}</td>
              <td><b>{b.oneEdition.median}</b></td>
              <td class="fine">{b.editionsWithArticle.allFourPc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Both columns rise at every step. Summed, the top band is
      {' '}{d.ladder.summed.fromTo}× the bottom; measured on one edition it is
      {' '}<b>{d.ladder.oneEdition.fromTo}×</b>. The gap between those two multiples is the part of
      the raw ladder that was coverage rather than reading. We report the smaller one.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {d.whyNotMatchOnEditions}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the ladder does not say</h2>
    <p>
      A median is a fact about a group. Readers usually want a fact about a person, and those are
      different sizes. So we also measured the one that answers the second question: take one actor
      from the top band and one from the bottom band at random, and how often is the busier one the
      more-read one?
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Measured on</th><th>Top band outreads bottom band</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="nm">One edition only</td><td><b>{한판확률}%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="nm">Summed across editions</td><td>{합확률}%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">{d.personLevel.whatItIs} {d.personLevel.whatFiftyMeans}</p>
    <p>
      <strong>So the bands overlap, heavily.</strong> Of the {겹.lowBandN} actors with a single
      charting title, <b>{겹.lowBandAboveHighMedian}</b> ({겹.lowBandAbovePc}%) are read more than
      the median actor with five or more. Going the other way,
      {' '}<b>{겹.highBandBelowLowMedian}</b> of {겹.highBandN} actors with five or more
      ({겹.highBandBelowPc}%) are read less than the median actor with one. A seven-times gap
      between the middles is not a rule about people at the edges.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Which way does it run?</h2>
    <p>
      We do not know, and nothing on this page can settle it. More charting titles may bring more
      readers. Being read may be what gets an actor cast again. Something we have not measured —
      an agency, a network, a single breakout year — may drive both. All three would produce the
      table above.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      We have measured the neighbouring question before: whether a title travelling to more
      countries goes with more lookups. That is on
      {' '}<a href="/actor-reach">how far a title travelled</a>, and it has the same limit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How the bands were cut</h2>
    <p class="note">{d.bandsAreOurs}</p>
    <p class="note">
      Every median on this page survives removing any single actor from its band, which rules out
      one way it could be fragile and does not show that it is stable. The check is a jackknife,
      which is known to understate how much a median moves, so a swing it finds is real while a
      swing it misses may be one it cannot see. The
      {' '}<a href="/one-out">method and its limits are here</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note">{d.panelCaveat}</p>
    <p class="note">
      Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews API, human traffic only, {d.window}. Cast and charting titles —
      Wikidata and Netflix country charts. Reads are expressed per million reads of that edition,
      so a small Wikipedia is not penalised for being small.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwCardnews set="works" count={5} />

  <KcwShorts set="works"
    says={`Fourteen seconds: the ladder of median reads by number of charting titles, the `
      + `chance one actor from the top band outreads one from the bottom, and where the two `
      + `bands overlap.`} />

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/works-and-readers" />
  <KcwMethodLimits method={d.method} limitation={d.limitation} />
  {/* 🔴 2026-08-22 — «왜 판별로 갈랐나»(whySplitByEdition)와 어느 판을 썼나(editions)를
      세어 두고 안 보여 주고 있었다. 갈라 센 까닭을 안 적으면 이 표는 그냥 순위표로 읽힌다 */}
  <section class="src">
    <h2>Why this is split by Wikipedia edition</h2>
    <p class="note">{d.whySplitByEdition}</p>
    <p class="note">
      The editions used here are {d.editions.join(', ')} — {d.editions.length} of them, each counted
      on its own so that an actor is not rewarded for simply appearing in more of them.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
